---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `The health unit wants a BMI calculator that also says which
category the number falls in. Weight in pounds and height in
inches, because that is what people actually know about
themselves.`;

const SampleOutput = `Weight (lbs): 150
Height (inches): 68

BMI: 22.8
Category: Normal weight`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="./cc-set-2" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 2
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: BMI Calculator</h1>

        <p>
          <span class="badge text-bg-warning">Extra Credit</span>
          <span class="ms-2 text-body-secondary"
            >Not part of the five required for this set.</span
          >
        </p>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="./cc-set-2">Set 2</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>The imperial formula is BMI = 703 &times; weight &divide; height&sup2;. Height squared means height times height.</li>
            <li>Report the BMI to one decimal place, then the category on a separate line.</li>
            <li>The category boundaries are published values. Look them up rather than guessing, and say where you found them in your requirements list.</li>
            <li>This challenge is two programs stacked: a calculation and a classification. Get the number right first.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={SampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">200 lbs at 70 inches is 28.7, and 120 lbs at 64 inches is 20.6. Check both.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-bmi-calculator</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
